{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1477461-the-dream-of-dreams-what-do-you-want-from-the-dreaming-the-astral","id":1477461,"title":"The Dream of Dreams-What Do You Want from the Dreaming/the Astral?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-26T12:07:56-07:00","id":1477461,"title":"The Dream of Dreams-What Do You Want from the Dreaming/the Astral?","content":"<div align=\"center\"><i>\u2033\u2018So I wasn\u2019t dreaming, after all,\u2019 she said to herself, \u2018unless \u2013 unless we\u2019re all part of the same dream. Only I do hope it\u2019s my dream, and not the Red King\u2019s! I don\u2019t like belonging to another person\u2019s dream,\u2019 she went on in a rather complaining tone: \u2018I\u2019ve a great mind to go and wake him, and see what happens!\u2018\u201d </i><br /> -Lewis Carroll, Through the Looking Glass</div> <br /> I've been meaning to start this conversation for a little bit now, but I didn't want to start a conversation without contributing to it as a start. But life is busy, and I don't want to delay kicking the hornet's nest and possibly never do it because of other obligations, so I will try and provide my takes later on, but for now:<br /> <br /> One of the biggest things that was lacking in the Beast's core was a actual inclusion and thorough exploration of the Astral, which I'm going to collectively call the Dreaming for the purposes of this Beast conversation, and what it meant for Beast as a game on it's own terms. The Player's Guide covered the basics of it in a pretty satisfactory way, but that does leave an open door into what more could be done or refigured.<br /> <br /> So, with that in mind, what do you want to see done with the Dreaming in regards to Beast going forward (both in normal and weird ways), how do you want it to factor into the games Beasts can play/tell, and why do you want those things?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T12:19:58-07:00","id":1477462,"title":"","content":"I know very little about Beast. How would Beasts interact with the landscape of the Temenos?<br /> <br /> Actually, isn\u2019t the Primordial Dream supposed to be the oldest and most primal region of the Temenos?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T12:28:16-07:00","id":1477465,"title":"","content":"Some examination of how Dreamborn interact between realms and layers of the Dreams \u2014 whether that's culture clash literalizing itself in the Temenos or Oneiroi being subverted by ideas from the wider world or the beastly archetypes of the Mother's Land reflecting themselves into the collective human unconscious, an examination of the Astral in the Begotten's more continuum-based view would help with its presentation as an otherworld.<br /> <br /> Also, a fresh look at stuff like Dreamborn from the Bright Dream being able to engage in ideological attacks (now that Dream Forms don't use Willpower as Health) and scenes in the Oneiros being able to try and impose their emotional context onto visitors feels like it would be useful for reframing how Nightmares function.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T12:36:23-07:00","id":1477467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1477461-the-dream-of-dreams-what-do-you-want-from-the-dreaming-the-astral?p=1477462#post1477462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know very little about Beast. How would Beasts interact with the landscape of the Temenos?<br /> <br /> Actually, isn\u2019t the Primordial Dream supposed to be the oldest and most primal region of the Temenos?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much correct. The Primordial Dream is the region that borders the barrier of language that seperates humanity from the other animals (expressed either through the Omphalos or the Cave, depending on which blind is leading the other blind), and is basically the realm where the primal instincts gain voice, form, shape, description-and since we're in a horror game, the reconciliation of fear is a big part of it's makeup.<br /> <br /> The Beast's Player Guide does a good job exploring the basic ideas from Primordial's point of view, which grafts onto what you might learn with Mage Second's core and adjoining sourcebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T13:19:28-07:00","id":1477472,"title":"","content":"I feel like Beast is sort of where Lost was in 1e regarding this: if you read all the books you have a good grasps of the metaphysical layout of things, a few story hooks, but not necessarily the interactivity and goals needed to really drive players to want to make exploration of this part of the game an active part of the story. There's enough meat on the bones that if your group is predisposed to wanted to explore the Dreaming, you know what's there and the basics, but I've never seen a Beast player that wasn't coming in interested in the Dreaming get hooked by that material as a reason to go dream hopping at some point (I will admit, that even applies to me a bit).<br /> <br /> So I think some stronger integrations into the core gameplay loops might be in order. The two big &quot;rewards&quot; for diving into the Dreaming are things you can do without going there. You can claim Chambers (assuming you have slots for more, and ones there don't inherently offer things you can't get locally), and you can perform minor acts of influence on human populations (at lot of the examples are things Beasts inclined towards social engineering on that level can probably get done with their Atavisms and/or judicious use of Nightmares as it is).<br /> <br /> I feel like the PG is actually a bit backwards here. Instead of being an alternate path to goals, the Dreaming should be a way to plant seeds; esp. with the idea of refocusing the game as a whole towards building up your character's myth. Instead of finding Chambers or being able to poison a town against a beloved local figure temporarily, it fees like Beasts that master the Dreaming should be setting up things: creating and nurturing urban legends that can then be used to empower Chamber creations, starting rumors about someone that isolates them and weakens them to the Nightmares you're going to inflict on them, being able to engage in a loop of finding the impact of your actions on a community in the Dreaming and then fine-tuning it over and over to write your legend just the way you want it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T14:15:18-07:00","id":1477477,"title":"","content":"I agree with what's been said until now. There is also an implication I feel bubbling the surface and I want to make it explicit: Future exploration of this topic ought to be combined with a Lore system. Begotten, Forsworn (Arc's take on Heroes) and Insatiables should all be able to affect the zeitgeist of their territories - be those territories local, or conceptual. There should be feedback loops between she shape of the Dreaming, events in the material, and aforementioned characters' personal Legends.<br /> <br /> I even had an out there idea, where since Beasts no longer possess an Oneiros, their personal Goetia may show up in the wider Astral, tied to various narratives, open to interference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T14:40:15-07:00","id":1477480,"title":"","content":"I am a simple person. I just want weird anomalies and strange entities which are not easily explained that mess around in the Astral, be it mysteries of the Dark Mother, decaying Lairs of ancient Apex of the past which maintain themselves by becoming legends or invasions of Heroic legacies which disrupt the Primordial Dream. Just give me the weird stuff and I'll be happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T14:58:39-07:00","id":1477481,"title":"","content":"Well, this is a topic near to my heart, since I believe that the Begotten\u2019s easy access to the Dreaming would be just as impactful as the Shadow, or the Underworld is on the Forsaken and Bound, if not more so. The Dreaming covers everything from specific dreams, to the dreams of humanity at large, and the very dreams of the world, and the Begotten have amazing access to all of it. Beasts can watch as simple words rip apart and rearrange the Dreaming, which is the kind of thing that makes one sit up and pay attention.<br /> <br /> In no particular order or relevance;<br /> <br /> A look at the exploration, and usage of personal nightmares. Beasts already can inflict bad dreams with a touch, what happens when one is actually inside someone\u2019s dreams? Why would ever the Begotten chose to do so, since personal dreams are probably one of the most stifling places to be for a Beast. (Being extremely uncomfortable in a dream just conjecture, but dreams usually are extremely narrative, and someone particularly sensitive to narratives probably won\u2019t appreciate being forcefully made into a symbol different from what they are.) If nothing else, it seems like a good place to feed and to study new Nightmares. (Maybe it uses a system like Oneiromancy from Changeling, with a Beast take on it of course) (I would like the Nightmare Shamans to truck with personal nightmares as much as Humanity\u2019s collective nightmares. Plus, dreams are just interesting)<br /> <br /> Some clear description on how feeding from the Dreaming works and messes with the waking world might be nice. And visa versa.<br /> <br /> A realm representing Heroism that is constantly attempting to wage war on the Primordial Dream. I believe this idea has come up before, but it\u2019s a good one. (Kinda something that feels like that should already be there, to be honest.)<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the attention of a Hero also attracting the attention of minor raiding parties of Heroic Dreamborn to harry the Horror and the Lair, and maybe act as a early warning system for heroic tracking. All without the Hero knowing a thing, of course. (Heroes don\u2019t seem that strong, but I think it\u2019s kind thematic that they cause way more trouble than they understand. Plus it\u2019s a way of even benevolent Heroes causing the Begotten some trouble.)<br /> <br /> Maybe a mention of a Collector or team of Collectors who steal stuff from the Oneiros\u2026like maybe stealing someone\u2019s distorted desires. (Someone might have gained a new crush on a game while waiting for Elden Ring. Maybe.)<br /> <br /> and I love what everyone has described so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T15:23:45-07:00","id":1477483,"title":"","content":"With all the talk of lore-shaping, I wonder if there\u2019s stuff we can borrow from Mage: The Ascension. You know, Foci and Reality Zones and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T16:42:32-07:00","id":1477488,"title":"","content":"Talking again about the Astral continuum: There's a few different things from the Astral pre-dating Beasts that the Begotten share conceptual ground with, such as\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2022 Nightmare creatures from the Oneiros, who inhabit nightmare scenes with no scripted temporal endpoint and instead torment anyone who enters their territory until they escape.<br /> \u2022 Chimerical beasts from the Temenos (described in Secrets of the Ruined Temple) \u2014 forgotten gods and terrifying monsters incarnating across the bridge of a human soul.<br /> \u2022 Naturae from the Anima Mundi, who are the rulers of the lands whose ecosystems they represent as well as those lands themselves \u2014 and their component creatures can turn against them.<br /> <br /> Comparatively rare as the Begotten are, it might be good to reexamine some of these in the context of Kinship and/or Hunger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T16:43:38-07:00","id":1477489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1477461-the-dream-of-dreams-what-do-you-want-from-the-dreaming-the-astral?p=1477483#post1477483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all the talk of lore-shaping, I wonder if there\u2019s stuff we can borrow from Mage: The Ascension. You know, Foci and Reality Zones and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div> Can you expound on this? I know little of Ascension besides some small scraps about the Consensus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T17:55:07-07:00","id":1477493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1477461-the-dream-of-dreams-what-do-you-want-from-the-dreaming-the-astral?p=1477489#post1477489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Can you expound on this? I know little of Ascension besides some small scraps about the Consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, me too \u2014 I\u2019m at the cupping point where I know just enough to daydream about it, but not enough to teach someone about it. But others will surely know better\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T18:22:23-07:00","id":1477495,"title":"","content":"Building on what Heavy Arms said, Beasts have a particularly direct relationship with the concept of narrative as something with real metaphysical weight, and I want to see more exploration of their unusual status as stories in the active process of telling themselves. Beasts may no longer be human, but the residual humanity that they do have put them in the unusual position of at least theoretically being able to consider what their story looks like from an outside perspective, what they <i>want</i> their story to be, and how they might bridge the gap.<br /> <br /> If Beast is a game about the story you tell about yourself against the story the world wants to tell about you then the various layers of the Dreaming are a battlefield where canny Beasts should be able to tilt the narrative. I want to see wordcount devoted to how a Beast might... recontextualize themselves. How to not simply grow your legend, but <i>shape</i> it. How you choose to feed, how the broader community understands the legend of a monster in its midst, that should shape how the horror grows and evolves.<br /> <br /> ...Hm, having typed the above I've finally made a connection that's been eluding me. The introduction to atavisms discusses how Horrors learn new ones, and cites contact with other Beasts as the most common way; The dragon learns to swim from the kraken, and so on. We're told Horrors change as they learn new atavisms, that like dreams they are malleable, but we aren't given other examples of how this happens and there isn't much discussion of this potential for dramatic alteration outside the context of learning new atavisms. There's a mention elsewhere that Hunger can change in extreme circumstances but... It feels like there are pieces pointing toward the idea that a sufficiently motivated Beast could, over time, eventually grow their Horror into something substantially different from what it started as and mucking about in the Dreaming seems like the likeliest path to doing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T18:26:50-07:00","id":1477497,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how much there really is to borrow from Ascension... it's a part of Ascension's systems that are pretty light and loose. The effects of things like Reality Zones are already built into how different areas of the Dreaming have different mechanics to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T22:22:04-07:00","id":1477519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1477461-the-dream-of-dreams-what-do-you-want-from-the-dreaming-the-astral?p=1477465#post1477465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some examination of how Dreamborn interact between realms and layers of the Dreams \u2014 whether that's culture clash literalizing itself in the Temenos or Oneiroi being subverted by ideas from the wider world or the beastly archetypes of the Mother's Land reflecting themselves into the collective human unconscious, an examination of the Astral in the Begotten's more continuum-based view would help with its presentation as an otherworld.<br /> <br /> Also, a fresh look at stuff like Dreamborn from the Bright Dream being able to engage in ideological attacks (now that Dream Forms don't use Willpower as Health) and scenes in the Oneiros being able to try and impose their emotional context onto visitors feels like it would be useful for reframing how Nightmares function.</div> </div> </div> </div>Long time ago I mentioned something like this, and am happy to see you want it too.<br /> <br /> In a way completely different from the Shadow or Awakened realms, I feel the Astral should be like a monstrous kingdom of ideas. This isn't the brutish and wild hunts of the Shadow, but a sprawling territory of fiefs and lairs filled with beings seeking to prove the superiority of the ideological concepts they represent. They effect the physical world in a subtle way unlike the shadow. The Astral effects the physical in such a way where it's mindsets that are effected. Over time, people find themselves not trusting democracy due to the actions of a dreamborn representing the fear of mob rule the populace developed from riots earlier that year, or a serial killer finds that, due to how he is being perceived and the developing mythology around him, he feels a certain power coursing within him (which is actually the very dreamborn representing him seeking to claim him)<br /> <br /> And the reverse is true. The Astral finds many new citizens coming from the thoughts and dreams of the physical. Phobias, aspirations, pop culture figures and all kinds find life here, and seek to prove themselves fit for rule to stay in the minds and hearts of the populace (whether that populace be the mind of the very person who conceived them, or the masses).<br /> <br /> Very important that they aren't the ideals the supernal represent, or the predatory and alien spirits that seek only to get essence. These are living ideas that represent not absolute truths or animistic concepts that only understand the next meal, but biases and wants and dreams and fears born DIRECTLY from Humanity. They wish to rule conquer the dream realms they inhabit so that they may be the primary force driving individual's (or masses of individuals). And for a Beast, this means they have a Kingdom of their own through their Lairs, so that they may prove themselves as worthy to exist as they self actualize themselves in the mind and soul of humanity.<br /> <br /> Until, of course, a Hero comes along to prove that, in truth, they are a false being who deserves to be forgotten","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T09:54:58-07:00","id":1477531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1477461-the-dream-of-dreams-what-do-you-want-from-the-dreaming-the-astral?p=1477519#post1477519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Long time ago I mentioned something like this, and am happy to see you want it too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to be clear: it's evident that the vast majority of Temenotic activity is self-contained and representational \u2014 the Bright Dream does not have to be concerned about geography the way the Shadow does, and most Astral beings are completely unconcerned with the material world if they are aware it exists.<br /> <br /> My interest is in having a little more detail given to how the described exceptions work; Astral Realms provides examples of means of transport between realms, including characters and vessels that specifically do so regularly; Naturae who lose control of their ecosystems are described as sometimes falling from the Dreamtime to the Swath or even to the Temenos as city-psyches; animals are stated to leave powerful psychic impressions the give rise to cultural imagery as well as the Animal Masters participating in the Dreamtime's great game of adaptation; the realms of the Temenos are thematically skewed but are flexible enough to incorporate visitors into their recurring stories, in contrast to the mnemonic scenes of the Oneiros; strange things like the Kindly Stranger reach into individual dreams to cast actors in uncanny pantomimes with consequences in the waking world; and of course everybody's daimon tries to steer them toward self-improvement.<br /> <br /> In general Mage 1e's perspective on the Astral, while distinct from the Begotten's view in ways that puts &quot;no neat little boxes&quot; front and center for the latter, is still the most detailed look we have at the Inner Realms and it probably shouldn't be rendered completely useless as a reference document when the biggest differences the Beast Player's Guide introduces are that the Begotten enter the Astral from the middle of the span, cut past most of the shallows of the Anima Mundi, and treat the entire Bright Dream like the Temenos once they make their way out of the Primordial Dream \u2014 Beasts are explicitly less common than mages, and while having <i>more</i> Astral stuff to work with would be good, it probably shouldn't be a major chunk of their reactive storytelling compared to dealing with, y'know, <i>people</i>.<br /> <br /> Werewolves can deHarmonize into not being able to leave the Shadow, changelings can get caught up in the Thorns and/or become Goblin Queens, everyone wandering the Underworld is a long drop away from a permanent stint as a Ferryman, but the Begotten are sufficiently compartmentalized that the common Inheritances are easily accessible if they just want to forsake humanity and spend all their time as a living legend, since Chambers make the Primordial Dream easily accessible even before Soul Communion keeps the most comfortable part of that other world ready for you.<br /> <br /> The Dreaming teems with inner demons of all sorts, and they're mostly kept to their native hells as they should be. I just want a little more to work with as far as the roads between them and the travelers thereupon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T14:13:51-07:00","id":1477644,"title":"","content":"Well, and in Temenos everything that was ever dreamt and understood exists and will keep existing. So there is also all the knowledge of mankind, even one that was lost to common history. This should include past Beasts, as they were known by other Begotten and so many humans. And since they were so strong in The Dreaming in life, and had such a high impact on so many minds, there should be many who would be recreated as Dreamborn, before or after death. The same would happen with Heroes. So there would be whole societies of Heroes and Begotten existing in the Temenos.<br /> <br /> Begotten societies would hold knowledge that was lost to the current ones, and also have a vested interest to interfere in reality, as the greater quantity of accomplished Beasts and Heroes would generate more Dreamborn. Real Begotten would have the mobility that the Dreamborn do not have, and also abilities that the dream creatures do not have, so there would be a lot of give-and-take between living and dreamed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T15:06:31-07:00","id":1477647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1477461-the-dream-of-dreams-what-do-you-want-from-the-dreaming-the-astral?p=1477644#post1477644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, and in Temenos everything that was ever dreamt and understood exists and will keep existing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Realms and Dreamborn disappear all the time. The Dreaming is chaotic, shifting constantly. Only while people still dream of something does it exist with the Dreaming, and Stone and Paper have better memories than people\u2026The only permanent things are concepts universal to Humanity. (If you are thinking of the Akashic Records, that\u2019s probably in the Supernal. The Collective Unconscious is not the same thing.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T11:00:14-07:00","id":1477690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1477461-the-dream-of-dreams-what-do-you-want-from-the-dreaming-the-astral?p=1477647#post1477647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Realms and Dreamborn disappear all the time. The Dreaming is chaotic, shifting constantly. Only while people still dream of something does it exist with the Dreaming, and Stone and Paper have better memories than people\u2026The only permanent things are concepts universal to Humanity. (If you are thinking of the Akashic Records, that\u2019s probably in the Supernal. The Collective Unconscious is not the same thing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum, even the Dreamborn are created and destroyed all the time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T11:48:19-07:00","id":1477695,"title":"","content":"(Disclaimer: I\u2019m not perfect, and if someone comes in to correct me, please listen to them. Also, we should probably move this conversation to the simple questions thread.)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1477461-the-dream-of-dreams-what-do-you-want-from-the-dreaming-the-astral?p=1477690#post1477690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hum, even the Dreamborn are created and destroyed all the time?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. And some are reborn in a new form, or pop back into existence as if nothing ever happened. Sometimes, it doesn\u2019t even have to be forgotten.<br /> Mind you, some don\u2019t. The Realm of Death is stable, and probably will remain so for a very long time. Many of it\u2019s denizens have probably been around basically since the Dreaming was a thing. As I understand, the more fundamental a realm to humanity or Dreamborn is, the more stable it is. But that doesn\u2019t mean it can\u2019t change radically. Let me ask you a question: what do you think order looks like? Some would say it looks like clockwork, or another type of machine. Others would say it looks like a city, or a particular kind of building like a courthouse, perhaps even a temple. So that\u2019s what a realm would look like, some combination of those thing, depending on that image\u2019s prominence in the human mind. A being from that realm probably resembles something orderly. Symmetry, functionality, and bureaucratic are common associations. But that\u2019s changed of the course of history. People change what they thought the concept was. Once, Order was drawn from chaos. It once was a home, a cave, a monument against the storm and sea. Then came came cities and civilization and the whole realm changed. Some parts have stayed. Some parts have vanished, and will never be seen again. And some may return, someday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T13:14:19-07:00","id":1477697,"title":"","content":"Created and destroyed is also probably a bit too harsh of a way to think about it. The BPG refers to this as the Mists: a state of amorphous existence where detail and vibrancy fade into a haze of indistinct dream shapes. Something that's moved into the Mists can be rescued from them, but there's not assurance that the reconstituted sureness of its new form is the same as what it was before it went it. While there is certainly room for a Ship of Theseus style debate on a Dreamborn fading and coming back different, there is frequently a continuity of existence involved rather than complete destruction and (re)invention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T13:59:28-07:00","id":1477702,"title":"","content":"Going back to my proposition, Beasts who became Dreamborn could be relatively stable, as the 'shared realms are relatively stable' (BPG 154). The realms that suffer constant change are the realms of an individual. Anyway, there are gods and demons from the astral that are stable enough for our purposes.<br /> <br /> And the 'relatively stable' part would work to give them a reason to interfere in reality. Fear of Beasts from humans in the real world would make their concept more stable and add another reason for them to associate with real Beasts. For simplicity's sake, I'd say that Dreamborn Beasts would live in regions that would be versions of their native cities, only closer to the conceptual dream-space of Fear. Original horrors unfettered by inheritance could be a big problem, as they would not only be would not be flattered by the imitations but would usually be stronger than the Dreamborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T15:05:08-07:00","id":1477709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1477461-the-dream-of-dreams-what-do-you-want-from-the-dreaming-the-astral?p=1477702#post1477702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going back to my proposition, Beasts who became Dreamborn could be relatively stable, as the 'shared realms are relatively stable' (BPG 154). The realms that suffer constant change are the realms of an individual. Anyway, there are gods and demons from the astral that are stable enough for our purposes.<br /> <br /> And the 'relatively stable' part would work to give them a reason to interfere in reality. Fear of Beasts from humans in the real world would make their concept more stable and add another reason for them to associate with real Beasts. For simplicity's sake, I'd say that Dreamborn Beasts would live in regions that would be versions of their native cities, only closer to the conceptual dream-space of Fear. Original horrors unfettered by inheritance could be a big problem, as they would not only be would not be flattered by the imitations but would usually be stronger than the Dreamborn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts won't become Dreamborn. There could be Dreamborn based on their Legends, but those would be separate entities distinct from the Unfettered Horrors of those who've undergone the Retreat, and, given the way Begotten powers work, probably wouldn't even resemble the Horrors. Being the collective idea of people who aren't Beasts, they'd have no more awareness of the nature of the Bright Dream than their mortal counterparts \u2014 the public image of someone who engages in the kind of behavior that the Hungers represent doesn't imply transdimensional conquest to the average mortal.<br /> <br /> The Temenos is a closely-connected network of realms and sub-realms of shared narrative, and the Begotten mostly deal with the fucked-up basement realm where breaking points and stage hazards live \u2014 realms of collective trauma may be likely to have Themes that connect to a Beast's Lair, but the Begotten generally approach stability by having a frightening pocket dimension that people aren't inclined to go near where their soul's supposed to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T20:40:46-07:00","id":1492197,"title":"","content":"A deeper look at what the astral beings can do would interesting. Could a Dreamborn with some relationship with greed could inflict a desire for money the same way a Beast does a Nightmare?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T13:17:50-07:00","id":1494547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1477461-the-dream-of-dreams-what-do-you-want-from-the-dreaming-the-astral?p=1492197#post1492197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A deeper look at what the astral beings can do would interesting. Could a Dreamborn with some relationship with greed could inflict a desire for money the same way a Beast does a Nightmare?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they have an appropriate Numia or Influence, I'd think so?<br /> Seems to be within their wheelhouse, but generally I don't think Dreamborn get many opportunities.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T09:18:53-08:00","id":1501954,"title":"","content":"I'd really love if beings entirely unrelated to the Beast Hero Insatiable trio might become like them and join with a human. Meaning sometimes a human is &quot;devoured&quot; not by a horror but by an Astral being that has nothing to do with fear it becomes a Beast whose &quot;horror&quot; is something different","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}